      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
      "created_at": "2025-01-08T01:43:38.257Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Honestly, I think that’s an issue that applies to a lot of Sentinel’s characters. It seems to me that far more of them have simple single-word names than “Something-Man or The Something or The Adjective Noun”-type names. E.g., Legacy, Tempest, Tachyon, etc. Granted, they do have some amount of  the latter type (e.g. The Wraith, The Argent Adept, Captain Cosmic), but the ratio seems much smaller than “real” companies. Part of this may very well be because many of the Word-Man type names were already taken.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2025-01-08T01:44:12.889Z",
