    {
      "id": 261934,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2025-01-08T13:13:06.666Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Personally, I just assume it’s a different universe where things happened a little differently. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/person_shrugging.png?v=12\" title=\":person_shrugging:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":person_shrugging:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> We already have various examples of things that were different, such as earlier lesbian representation. I just chalk it up to that. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"fjur\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"31254\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/48/4849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fjur:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Part of this may very well be because many of the Word-Man type names were already taken.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Oh, 100%. And this is why I’m fine with the weird names: GTG has a lot of constraints that the actual comics did not have.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2025-01-08T13:15:27.398Z",
